    {
      "hash": "4da68c4206caeed8cf5065cb8d123eb498da96d28d8d5a830235d1badd4b6ff5",
      "id": "id-0",
      "locator": {
        "anchor": "el-0",
      },
      "text": "Retrieval practice beats re-reading. The classic result is worth restating in one line: forcing recall, then getting feedback, is what moves an item from short-term recognition to long-term [recall](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Recall_\\(memory\\)).",
      "type": "paragraph",
    },
    {
      "hash": "1f6d0594cbae394785b2df6cf850d2cbaaf7dcbf1a865f293cd0a7ca37dd1a0a",
      "id": "id-3",
      "locator": {
        "anchor": "el-2",
      },
      "text": "The interval between reviews should grow every time you get the item right. The classic curve is the exponential-ish forgetting curve; a single review's expected stability change is often written as $E=mc^2$, which mangles nothing here because it is the point: an inline formula must survive.",
      "type": "paragraph",
    },
    {
      "hash": "d1a2ca75aa5285b33ad21dad3f702965244b8950c570469dd69166dfeeaf80bc",
      "id": "id-4",
      "locator": {
        "anchor": "el-3",
      },
      "text": "See the note on measured effect sizes[1](#fn:1) for the numbers behind this.",
      "type": "paragraph",
    },
    {
      "hash": "b39af9fb9e63d2e1e76624b89cf730e360a4fd5678d1abb6c7741d12f38d26ae",
      "id": "id-6",
      "locator": {
        "anchor": "el-5",
      },
      "text": "Integrating the forgetting curve over one interval gives the expected retrievability:",
      "type": "paragraph",
    },
    {
      "hash": "91394f922af3cad2c92e0ea24c3f84372692daff9bcc5a1a950b6a2c13150206",
      "id": "id-7",
      "locator": {
        "anchor": "el-6",
      },
      "text": "$$\\int_0^1 x^2\\,dx$$",
      "type": "equation",
    },
    {
      "hash": "0ab20f606a87fabd155229767d40c7d524e892d7d0c33b273db6b9034d567684",
      "html": "<pre><code class="language-python" data-lang="python">def next_interval(stability, difficulty):
    return stability * (1 - difficulty / 10)</code></pre>",
      "id": "id-8",
      "locator": {
        "anchor": "el-7",
      },
      "text": "def next_interval(stability, difficulty):
    return stability * (1 - difficulty / 10)",
      "type": "code",
    },
    {
      "hash": "5b0dc77c5c4cfad622a0b98c2702da5fb06052ce539e013c843ed14581a86df4",
      "id": "id-10",
      "locator": {
        "anchor": "el-9",
      },
      "text": "A diagram of the review cycle:",
      "type": "paragraph",
    },
    {
